**POLICE SUMMARY — CCTV FOOTAGE, CAM16_STREAM-16 (Visat T Junction)**
**Period covered:** 22 minutes, 13-06-2026 (Saturday), 14:47:23 to 15:08:53

**1. SCENE**
Camera cam16_stream-16 overlooks Visat T Junction from an elevated position, with the overlay "Visat T Junction P2 RLVD" visible throughout. The view covers a signalised T-junction with a zebra crossing in the foreground, a raised central traffic island (with ONGC/IOCL-branded signage, kiosks and hoardings at various points), an ONGC facility to the right, an HP fuel station area visible on the far side (minute 3), a blue-hoarded footpath on the left, and a blue "Reliance" sign on the right (minute 14). A large red billboard is visible on the far side in several clips. All footage is night-time, lit by streetlights, traffic signals, illuminated billboards/shopfronts and vehicle headlights, with typical low-light glare, bloom and motion blur. Road surface appears damp/reflective in minutes 2–3; lanes described as dry in minute 15.

**2. TRAFFIC AND PEOPLE**
Traffic was steady and mixed throughout all 22 minutes:
- **Two-wheelers:** the dominant vehicle class, estimated 15–20+ per minute, rising to an estimated 30–40 in minute 21. Most riders wore light/white clothing; helmets noted where resolvable.
- **Auto-rickshaws:** yellow-and-green and yellow-topped autos present in every minute, typically 4–8 per clip.
- **Cars:** approx. 8–15 per clip, predominantly white, plus black, silver/grey, red, maroon, dark red, dark blue and one orange/amber SUV-type car (minute 8). SUVs, hatchbacks, sedans, MPVs and vans noted; a white boxy off-road-style SUV with dark roof at minute 8 (39–45s), an SUV with rear-mounted spare wheel at minute 11 (~35s).
- **Buses:** red city bus (minute 3, ~0–15s, and minute 13, 44–54s), red-roofed public bus (minute 3, ~45s), red-and-white city bus (minutes 4, 10), blue-and-white city bus (minutes 2, 13), blue-and-orange bus (minutes 7, 15), yellow-and-blue city bus (minute 6), white coach/bus (minutes 0, 2 with "SHREE" on rear, 20), light blue and white buses (minute 16), blue-roofed and red/orange buses (minute 18), white bus/minibus and red-and-cream van/minibus (minute 10).
- **Trucks/vans:** white open-body mini truck (minute 4, ~20s), red truck (minute 4, ~40s), white low-bed truck carrying another vehicle (minute 6), white van/SUV (minutes 4, 6, 7, 17, 20), white goods/carry-style three-wheeler (minute 19, ~45s), dark goods truck (minute 17, ~5s), white truck/van on right approach (minute 15), cement mixer truck (minute 16).
- **Special:** white ambulance/police-type van with active blue-red emergency lights, entering ~34s and crossing right to left ~44–49s (minute 0).
- **Cyclists:** pale-shirted cyclist (minute 2, ~15–20s), cyclist crossing junction (minute 7), cyclist in white (minutes 10, 21, ~35–40s).
- **Pedestrians:** small numbers in nearly every minute — crossing the zebra, waiting at kerbs, standing near the island. Notable: woman in dark traditional dress standing at left kerb nearly the whole of minute 6; woman with child waiting from ~25s (minute 5); group of 2–3 crossing ~40–50s (minute 12); pedestrian standing in the carriageway near centre ~50–55s (minute 12); at least eight people crossing or waiting (minute 16); two people in white walking across the carriageway near the island ~10–15s (minute 5).

**3. VEHICLES IDENTIFIED**
None identified. (Night footage; no badges or makes/models legible in any minute.)

**4. REGISTRATIONS READ**
None legible. (No registration numbers were quoted in any minute.)

**5. NOTABLE EVENTS**
- Minute 0: white ambulance/police-type van with active blue-red emergency lights, entering ~34s and again crossing right to left ~44–49s. No associated incident observed.
- Minute 13: white open-back utility/pick-up style van with people riding in its rear (9–24s) — possible unsafe carriage of passengers.
- Minute 15: red/orange truck carrying several standing passengers in its open rear at ~45s — possible unsafe carriage of passengers.
No other suspicious or alert-worthy events observed.

**6. CROWD AND CONGESTION**
None observed. Traffic flowed steadily throughout; no queues, build-ups or jams recorded. Notable pedestrian presence at minutes 5, 6, 12 and 16, but no crowd build-up.

**7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS**
- Minute 9: at least one rider apparently unhelmeted (~5s), another near ~50s.
- Minute 14: many riders without visible helmets.
- Minute 12: pedestrian standing in the carriageway near the centre ~50–55s.
- Minutes 13 and 15: passengers riding in open vehicle rears (see Notable Events).
No wrong-way driving, red-light jumping or illegal parking observed (vehicles stopping on/near the crossing noted at minutes 8 and 3 but not confirmed as violations).

**8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY**
Conditions were consistently night-time with steady, free-flowing mixed traffic across all 22 minutes, dominated throughout by two-wheelers, followed by cars (mostly white) and yellow-green auto-rickshaws in every clip. Activity peaked in minute 21 (30–40 two-wheelers estimated) and was heaviest generally in the later minutes (19–21, described as "light-to-moderate" to "steady" with continuous flow); minute 10 was the only clip described as merely "moderate". Recurring elements: signal cycles between amber and red; pedestrians crossing the zebra in ones and twos in nearly every minute; buses of various liveries (red, blue-and-white, blue-and-orange) passing through at intervals; a car parked/static at the far-left edge throughout minute 19. No incident, congestion or disruption recurred; the period shows an ordinary busy night junction.

**9. QUIET PERIODS**
None observed. Every minute recorded continuous traffic; no stretch was free of activity.
